(7601498, 1227544, 109227, '<td valign="top">I thought this might be your''s Anita.  I really love the expression and freckles.</td>', 'I thought this might be your''s Anita.  I really love the expression and freckles.', '2018-11-08 08:25:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601499, 1227843, 30364, '<td valign="top">Hey Lev, sorry I didn''t make any comments in-challenge, but if I had I''d have spoken very enthusiastically about this.  I''ve tried a million times (well, perhaps not quite that many) to get a really good rain photograph.  Never got much to write home about.  Had I taken this, I''d have written home immediately.  It''s just what I had always hoped for and never managed, not even close.  It''s perfect.  Thank you!</td>', 'Hey Lev, sorry I didn''t make any comments in-challenge, but if I had I''d have spoken very enthusiastically about this.  I''ve tried a million times (well, perhaps not quite that many) to get a really good rain photograph.  Never got much to write home about.  Had I taken this, I''d have written home immediately.  It''s just what I had always hoped for and never managed, not even close.  It''s perfect.  Thank you!', '2018-11-08 08:34:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601500, 1227836, 60581, '<td valign="top">Thank you Rian! This is well known place for DPC GTG. We used to have a GTG every years or may be two and many known folks were use to join for this :)<br/> <br/>About the drop removal Yes I could have but I was not sure if that would have been allowed because that is not a sensor dust but actually something else.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RianBotes:</b></div><hr/><i> What a lovely setting and exposure handled well/well processed. These kind of shots inspire one to get back in to nature with camera and not simply walk through it. If possible, try and clone out that water droplet that most likely ended up on your lens. Happens to me and hate it when it happens. Congrats with the HM. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thank you Rian! This is well known place for DPC GTG. We used to have a GTG every years or may be two and many known folks were use to join for this :) About the drop removal Yes I could have but I was not sure if that would have been allowed because that is not a sensor dust but actually something else. Originally posted by RianBotes: What a lovely setting and exposure handled well/well processed. These kind of shots inspire one to get back in to nature with camera and not simply walk through it. If possible, try and clone out that water droplet that most likely ended up on your lens. Happens to me and hate it when it happens. Congrats with the HM. ', '2018-11-08 08:39:11.000000', NULL, 0),
