(7601626, 1227653, 185772, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the ribbon!</td>', 'Congrats on the ribbon!', '2018-11-08 21:14:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601669, 1227843, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very cool Lev, congratulations!  Was your camera exposed to this rain or was it protected?  Curious how good the weather sealing on camera and lens is!  I still haven''t jumped fully into M43...I have my older Panny G5 I''ve carried on a couple of trips, but never have used it for serious work.  The Oly''s always have tempted me, and the newer Panny''s too with IBIS.</td>', 'Very cool Lev, congratulations!  Was your camera exposed to this rain or was it protected?  Curious how good the weather sealing on camera and lens is!  I still haven''t jumped fully into M43...I have my older Panny G5 I''ve carried on a couple of trips, but never have used it for serious work.  The Oly''s always have tempted me, and the newer Panny''s too with IBIS.', '2018-11-08 23:16:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601681, 1228014, 98565, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Yo_Spiff:</b></div><hr/><i> Thag lerns to use magick pickchur box. Female grows old waiting for Thag to cumpose shot. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>haha, that is so funny!!!!!</td>', 'Originally posted by Yo_Spiff: Thag lerns to use magick pickchur box. Female grows old waiting for Thag to cumpose shot.   haha, that is so funny!!!!!', '2018-11-09 01:32:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601709, 1227320, 19959, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for the votes and comments... <br/>@Teafran - Thankyou for the comment, appreciated. I''m glad you like my interpretation of Santorini. <br/> <br/>I developed an HDR version of this composition which works well. I opened up the scene a little more and did some heavy cloning of some rooftops to simplify the scene. <br/></td>', 'Thanks all for the votes and comments... @Teafran - Thankyou for the comment, appreciated. I''m glad you like my interpretation of Santorini.  I developed an HDR version of this composition which works well. I opened up the scene a little more and did some heavy cloning of some rooftops to simplify the scene. ', '2018-11-09 03:57:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601792, 1227843, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neil:</b></div><hr/><i> Very cool Lev, congratulations!  Was your camera exposed to this rain or was it protected?  Curious how good the weather sealing on camera and lens is!  I still haven''t jumped fully into M43...I have my older Panny G5 I''ve carried on a couple of trips, but never have used it for serious work.  The Oly''s always have tempted me, and the newer Panny''s too with IBIS. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Neil, thank you! No, it wasn''t really exposed, I was mostly shooting from under the awnings. But I know for a fact that weather sealing on Olympus cameras and PRO lenses is amazing - I was once knocked down by a rogue wave in Iceland and washed all over with my camera "on" in my hands. The lenses in the bag were wet, too. Salty water and thin black sand. Everything survived!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-11-09 13:41:18.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Neil: Very cool Lev, congratulations!  Was your camera exposed to this rain or was it protected?  Curious how good the weather sealing on camera and lens is!  I still haven''t jumped fully into M43...I have my older Panny G5 I''ve carried on a couple of trips, but never have used it for serious work.  The Oly''s always have tempted me, and the newer Panny''s too with IBIS.  Neil, thank you! No, it wasn''t really exposed, I was mostly shooting from under the awnings. But I know for a fact that weather sealing on Olympus cameras and PRO lenses is amazing - I was once knocked down by a rogue wave in Iceland and washed all over with my camera "on" in my hands. The lenses in the bag were wet, too. Salty water and thin black sand. Everything survived!', '2018-11-09 13:39:41.000000', '2018-11-09 13:41:18.000000', 0),
(7601866, 1227700, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the blue, Neil. Beautiful work!</td>', 'Congratulations on the blue, Neil. Beautiful work!', '2018-11-09 23:27:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7601918, 1227544, 19825, '<td valign="top">Classic Anita. Beautifully done. I envy your child portrait skills.</td>', 'Classic Anita. Beautifully done. I envy your child portrait skills.', '2018-11-10 12:19:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7602106, 1227843, 97225, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the red, Lev. Great, evocative capture.<br/>After reading your notes I can really relate to this. My daughter''s wedding plans (beach wedding) had to be modified because of rain. 250mm over a few hours, but that rain was sideways. The next day was gorgeous and we faked the wedding shots on the beach.</td>', 'Congratulations on the red, Lev. Great, evocative capture.After reading your notes I can really relate to this. My daughter''s wedding plans (beach wedding) had to be modified because of rain. 250mm over a few hours, but that rain was sideways. The next day was gorgeous and we faked the wedding shots on the beach.', '2018-11-11 19:18:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7602292, 1227933, 193969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by JulietNN:</b></div><hr/><i> Absolutely brilliant, no idea how you managed this much sharpens on the blade, but it is brilliant. Love how you have brought the colours out, I am really enjoying looking at it, well done! 8 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The wind was flaky and inconsistent, which got the blades turning on their axis to maximize power generation.  The rotation caught the light differently in each of the 50 exposures I stacked into one final image in Photoshop.</td>', 'Originally posted by JulietNN: Absolutely brilliant, no idea how you managed this much sharpens on the blade, but it is brilliant. Love how you have brought the colours out, I am really enjoying looking at it, well done! 8   The wind was flaky and inconsistent, which got the blades turning on their axis to maximize power generation.  The rotation caught the light differently in each of the 50 exposures I stacked into one final image in Photoshop.', '2018-11-13 00:48:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7602430, 1227947, 185714, '<td valign="top">Thank you for your votes &amp; comments.<br/> <br/>Greatly appreciated.<br/> <br/>cheers<br/>gin</td>', 'Thank you for your votes & comments. Greatly appreciated. cheersgin', '2018-11-14 00:10:27.000000', NULL, 0);
